OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1774910894
OL,1,Vk4                               G5/9
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGKURDISH REBELS
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGAPPEAL TO UN
OL,4,D
OL,5, Kurdish rebels have appealed to the UN
OL,6, and the US-led coalition to intervene
OL,7, in the bitter fighting in northern Iraq
OL,9,FAfter claiming the recapture of Kirkuk,
OL,10,FKurdish forces said thousands of
OL,11,Fcivilians had been killed in reprisals
OL,12,Fby Saddam Hussein's troops.
OL,13,F
OL,14,F"What we are facing now is a campaign
OL,15,Fthat has all the hallmarks of genocide"
OL,16,Fsaid Kurdish leader Masoud Barzani.
OL,18,FThe US has reiterated that it would not
OL,19,Fintervene in fighting between Iraqi
OL,20,Ffactions, saying it had no mandate from
OL,21,Fthe United Nations to do so.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG30-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
